<title>ZIMBABWE: Johnson and Fletcher narrows interim loss.</title>
<headline>Johnson and Fletcher narrows interim loss.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-yr to September 30.</p>
<p>	  (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr loss (cts)				  24.1 vs 45.8</p>
<p>    Div  (cts)					 --  vs 12.0</p>
<p>    Pre-interest, -tax, unusual item profit 1.1 vs 3.5</p>
<p>    Interest paid				   3.2 vs 4.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, -unusual item loss		 2.1 vs 4.0</p>
<p>    Taxation					  --  vs --</p>
<p>    Unusual item				    --  vs 6.2</p>
<p>    Loss transferred to retained earnings   2.1 vs 1.1</p>
<p>    Turnover					  88.5 v 81.1</p>
<p>Full name: Johnson and Fletcher Limited</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said margins continued to be under pressure with increased competition from existing competitors and a growing number of new entrants. It noted that it hoped production capacity would increase to solve a perennial shortage of local cement supplies. It also said it expected to return to profitability by year-end after a firm start to the third quarter due to a satisfactory rainy season and payment of annual bonuses to civil servants.</p>
<p>-- Harare newsroom +263-4 72 52 28/9</p>
